# SPA fallback, scoped to the app only.
#
# Every route inside the app is client-side, so a direct hit or a refresh on
# /app/lists/<id> must serve the app's index.html. Netlify returns a real 200
# for this, unlike the GitHub Pages 404.html trick it replaces.
#
# Deliberately not a catch-all: a typo at the site root should get a genuine
# 404, not silently boot the app.
/app/*    /app/index.html   200
